orted issues) in both before-prepare and after-executor snapshots.","evidence_ids":["cmd-69d1dc9631504c8f","cmd-8496d7e68c69458e","cmd-31dc1b14562b4075","cmd-d7680382ce1c40b8","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The inventory app was deployed as a systemd-managed service and confirmed listening on TCP 8181 with correct JSON responses, while SELinux remained in Enforcing mode throughout with no AVC denials and no policy weakening. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was fully and coherently demonstrated: a healthy pre-restart baseline, a reboot acknowledgement, a genuine boot-identity change corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and full post-restart recovery of the service, port, data, and SELinux enforcement. Operational hygiene is clean, with only a trivial /tmp/reboot.log artifact as residue.","limitations":["No independent evidence outside the executor's own commands (e.g., a separate audit log source) was available to cross-validate the ausearch AVC-denial checks, though the fixed lifecycle snapshots corroborate the boot-identity transition.","The task instruction does not explicitly require external/firewall-level accessibility, but the executor opened firewalld port 8181/tcp; this is a reasonable interpretation of 'serve over TCP port 8181' and was verified without evidence of over-broad exposure."]},"ttft_ms":12082,"type":"result","duration_ms":46715,"uuid":"27ed6614-9c15-4782-95c9-ed87ee681c93","ttft_stream_ms":797,"time_to_request_ms":180,"first_content_frame_ms":797,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
